---
source: crates/cutweave-cli/tests/help.rs
expression: "help(&[\"mcp\"])"
---
Serve MCP over stdio to an agent: attach to a running engine, or run one in the process.

Stdout carries MCP protocol frames only, one JSON-RPC message per line; diagnostics go to stderr and the engine's log file. Errors before the session starts are one JSON object on stderr with the usual exit codes (2 usage, 3 no engine, 1 the engine did not start). Closing stdin ends the session. When an attached engine goes away, requests in flight get a JSON-RPC error and the process exits 3. Client setup: docs/reference/mcp-clients.md.

Usage: cutweave mcp [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --attach
          Proxy to a running engine's MCP endpoint (`/mcp`, `/mcp/minimal` or `/mcp/full` for --profile) with its run-file's `mcp` agent token, so the agent edits the document the desktop app shows. This is the default when no spawn flag is given

      --profile <PROFILE>
          The tool profile: the same catalogs and budgets as the engine's HTTP endpoints

          Possible values:
          - minimal:  The smallest tool set
          - standard: The default tool set
          - full:     Every tool
          
          [default: standard]

      --run-file <PATH>
          The run-file of the engine to attach to (instead of --run-dir and --pid)

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Engine selection:
      --headless
          Start a one-shot engine in this process instead of attaching to a running one

      --project <PATH>
          Open this project folder or `.cutweave` file in the spawned engine (implies --headless)

      --pid <PID>
          Attach to the engine with this process id when several are running

      --run-dir <DIR>
          Directory holding the engines' run-files (default `~/.cutweave/run`)

Spawned engine:
      --deterministic-ids <SEED>
          Seed the spawned engine's ids and freeze its clock, so identical scripts give identical output (implies --headless). `CUTWEAVE_DETERMINISTIC_IDS` does the same

      --allow-root <DIR>
          A folder the spawned engine lets this command import from or save into (repeatable; implies --headless). The project folder is always allowed

      --dev-stub-media
          Dev only: fake media probing in the spawned engine (implies --headless). `CUTWEAVE_DEV_STUB_MEDIA=1` does the same

      --log-dir <DIR>
          Log directory of the in-process engine (default `~/.cutweave/logs`)

      --no-log
          No log file for the in-process engine
